\f4\fs26 Damien had not even made it to the elevators when he heard the commotion. People were coming from every direction and heading for the Director\'92s Office in a mad panic. By the time he entered the office it was full of gawkers and office geeks, some of whom already had their hand-devices out and recording for a social media download. \
\'93All of you put the devices down down and get the fuck out of here!\'94 A couple of them looked around, but kept filming. \'93This means you fuck-face. Give me that phone.\'94 The reluctant office-dweeb failed to hand over the phone in a timely enough fashion and was thrown on his head by Damien in a serious attempt to break his neck. The phone dropped and was immediately crushed under foot. \'93Anyone else want to record this? Hand them over people.\'94 At that 10 devices hit the deck and were all subject the same fate as the first. \'93Get the fuck out. This is a crime scene.\'94\
Now alone he made a quick assessment of the scene. A was quite obviously a murder-suicide, but he could not fathom it. He had just been speaking to Janine not two minutes before and she seemed fine. She said she was looking forward to her son\'92s birthday, not more than a week away. Something was definitely wrong and decided he had better secure the room and let the cops work it out. This was way too big for an internal cover-up, the news would get out quickly.\
At that moment a hologram appeared on the Director\'92s desk, \'93Director? What happened? What\'92s going on there?\'94 The CEO inquired innocently.\
\'93The director has been shot by one of the secretaries. They are both dead.\'94 Damien said.\
\'93Who is that?\'94\
\'93Agent Damien Hardman, sir.\'94\
\'93I was just speaking to the director when we were cut off.\'94\
\'93It only just happened, sir. She seemed fine to me, but I can\'92t see how it could have happened any other way. She just walked in, shot him and then shot herself.\'94\
\'93Is there any way of keeping this in house?\'94 the CEO inquired, knowing full well that the news was already out.\
\'93No. I don\'92t think so. Half the admin-staff were taking vids when I walked in.\'94\
\'93Those recordings cannot get out.\'94 The CEO insisted.\
\'93It\'92s already sorted. Every device has been smashed, along with one of the camera men.\'94 He smiled proudly. It was yet another example of the problem solving properties of personal violence. \
\'93Good work. In fact I have heard nothing but good reports about you, Agent Hardman. I am promoting you. Clear out your desk, you are now the Director.\'94 \
 \
\'93Sir, I am amazed you have heard about me at all. I\'92d be jumping five pay grades. Are you certain you have the right man?\'94\
\'93Do you want the job or not, son? I don\'92t want to hear any of this false modesty nonsense. Take the job or risk disappointing me.\'94 The CEO knew that no one dared disappoint him.\
\'93Of course, sir. I can\'92t wait to see the looks of the Deputy Directors.\'94 Damien was now grinning wildly. The enormity of what had just happened was sinking in. He was the Director, the fuckin Director! 
\f5\i Oh, Yeah!\'85\'85.Oh, dear.
\f4\i0 \
\'93They\'92ll have their knives out.\'94\
\'93I\'92ll just sack them.\'94\
\'93You have the reigns. Do whatever you think is prudent to establish stability.\'94 The CEO was jubilant. He thought Damien must have been reading his mind. He had been planning a bit of a purge for a while now and his new director would bring the timetable forward. The Deputy Directors, each of whom commanded an army of operatives, would not go without a fight and there was the potential for civil war to erupt within Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Pro-active Euthanasia Directorate. He figured Damien would only last a week and any knowledge he had of the bombing would die with him. Whoever was left standing after the dust settled would be too shell-shocked to pose much of a threat to him and he or she would be his puppet.\
